---
/** Book I, Ch. II, Prop. 3 — the boundary turns toward the point it got wrong. */
---
<svg class="fig" viewBox="0 0 720 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="pu-t pu-d" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" style="--fig-min: 580px">
  <title id="pu-t">An update rotates the boundary toward the misclassified point</title>
  <desc id="pu-d">
    Before the update a positive point lies on the negative side. Adding y times
    x to the weight vector turns the weight vector toward that point, which
    swings the boundary until the point is on the correct side. Points already
    classified correctly produce no change at all.
  </desc>

  <text x="0" y="22" class="t-lab">before</text>
  <text x="380" y="22" class="t-lab">after one update</text>

  {/* LEFT panel */}
  <line x1="40" y1="250" x2="300" y2="82" class="wire" />
  <circle cx="120" cy="120" r="7" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="132" y="114" class="t-sm">x, y = +1</text>
  <text x="52" y="286" class="t-key" style="fill: var(--oxblood-text)">margin ≤ 0 — a mistake</text>
  {/* old w, pointing up-right from the line */}
  <line x1="170" y1="166" x2="228" y2="212" class="wire-soft" />
  <polygon points="222,203 238,221 219,222" class="head" />
  <text x="238" y="240" class="t-key">w</text>

  {/* divider */}
  <line x1="340" y1="60" x2="340" y2="280" class="dash" />

  {/* RIGHT panel: boundary rotated so the point is on the + side */}
  <line x1="420" y1="268" x2="700" y2="196" class="wire" />
  <circle cx="500" cy="120" r="7" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="512" y="114" class="t-sm">x, y = +1</text>
  <text x="432" y="300" class="t-key" style="fill: var(--verdigris)">margin &gt; 0 — correct</text>
  {/* new w rotated toward x */}
  <line x1="548" y1="230" x2="566" y2="160" class="wire" />
  <polygon points="558,166 570,146 574,166" class="head" />
  <text x="580" y="150" class="t-key">w + y·x</text>
  {/* the added vector, dashed */}
  <line x1="548" y1="230" x2="600" y2="272" class="dash" />
  <text x="606" y="286" class="t-xs">old w</text>

  <line x1="14" y1="46" x2="300" y2="46" class="wire-soft" />
  <line x1="380" y1="46" x2="706" y2="46" class="wire-soft" />

  <text x="0" y="316" class="t-xs">w ← w + y·x turns the normal toward the point; the boundary follows</text>
</svg>
